 69
DESCRIPTION:Friday 12/18 to Tuesday 12/22 · library hours\, ending 6:00 PM
  on 12/22 · local authors Monday 12/21 · 3:00 PM to 5:00 PM\n\nThe Mary 
 Esther Library borrows the Icelandic Christmas Eve tradition of Jolabokafl
 od\, the book flood\, when families give books and read with hot cocoa. Fr
 om Friday December 18 through 6:00 PM on Tuesday December 22\, visitors ge
 t free chocolate\, hot cocoa and books. Library card holders also take hom
 e a free book from the library bookstore. On Monday December 21 from 3:00 
 PM to 5:00 PM\, local authors sign and sell books for holiday gifts.\n\nPr
